      {
        "type": "Module",
        "name": "power_good_monitor",
        "description": "LM393 dual comparator module powered from VCC_3V3. Comparator channel 1 monitors the 3.3V rail and generates a POWER_GOOD status output based on a threshold set by an external passive network added later. Because LM393 outputs are open-drain, this module owns an open-drain POWER_GOOD interface and requires a pull-up destination to be defined in downstream implementation. The monitored rail is connected directly from the 3.3V provider to this module's sense input using the same VCC_3V3 net name for sensing intent. Comparator channel 2 is unused for system function; both 2IN_P and 2IN_N must be tied to GND, and 2OUT is left unused unless later terminated for stability policy.",
